{"id": 557, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark>n 18-month-old boy is evaluated for recurrent infections.\u00a0 He has been hospitalized 3 times with pneumonia since age 3 months.\u00a0 He has also had multiple skin infections requiring treatment with antibacterial and antifungal agents.\u00a0 During his last episode of pneumonia, he developed a large pleural effusion, which was drained.\u00a0 The pleural fluid revealed numerous neutrophils containing a large number of intact gram-positive cocci.\u00a0 The microorganisms responsible for this patient's recurrent infections most likely produce which of the following virulence factors?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Catalase"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Coagulase"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Lecithinase"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Lipopolysaccharide"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Polysaccharide capsule"}], "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T54946\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">C</mark>hronic granulomatous disease</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Pathogenesis</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">X-linked recessive mutation of NADPH oxidase</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Impaired respiratory burst &amp; \u2193 reactive oxygen species \u2192 inhibition of phagocytic intracellular killing</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Microbiology</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Catalase-positive organisms<ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"list-style-type: circle; font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Bacteria: <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Staphylococcus aureus, Burkholderia, Serratia, Nocardia</em></li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Fungi: <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Aspergillus</em></li></ul></li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Clinical features</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Recurrent infections of lungs, skin, liver, lymph nodes</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Diffuse granuloma formation</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Diagnosis</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Measurement of neutrophil superoxide production<ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"list-style-type: circle; font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">DHR flow cytometry (preferred)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">NBT testing</li></ul></li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">DHR</strong> = dihydrorhodamine; <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">NBT</strong> = nitroblue tetrazolium.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This infant with recurrent pulmonary and skin infections likely has a primary immunodeficiency disorder.\u00a0 The presence of a large number of intact bacteria inside the neutrophils suggests <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">chronic granulomatous disease</strong> (CGD), an X-linked recessive immunodeficiency marked by <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">impaired NADPH oxidase</strong> activity.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">NADPH oxidase resides on the plasma membrane of neutrophils and is incorporated into the membrane of the phagolysosome during phagocytosis; it catalyzes the formation of <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">superoxide free radicals</strong>, which subsequently destroy engulfed pathogens (eg, fungi, bacteria) as part of the <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-s7wj0v0tfn093y8d7blzrsc9\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-s7wj0v0tfn093y8d7blzrsc9\">oxidative burst</a>.\u00a0 Because patients with CGD have impaired NADPH oxidase activity, they are not able to efficiently destroy bacteria and fungi following <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-dgwirhnrrt9a3qymxn8s9p6o\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-dgwirhnrrt9a3qymxn8s9p6o\">phagocytosis</a>; therefore, microscopy will often reveal <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">intact microbes</strong> in the neutrophil phagolysosome during active infection.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Patients with CGD are most susceptible to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">catalase-positive organisms</strong>, particularly <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Staphylococcus aureus</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Burkholderia</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Serratia</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nocardia</em>, and <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Aspergillus</em>.\u00a0 Catalase degrades hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen, which reduces oxidative damage and protease activation by reactive oxygen species.\u00a0 Although most pathogenic bacteria and fungi produce catalase, catalase-positive organisms pose a particular risk to patients with CGD because they require higher levels of free radicals (ie, greater NADPH oxidase function) for effective killing.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">S aureus</em> produces coagulase, which binds to prothrombin and increases conversion of fibrinogen to fibrin.\u00a0 Fibrin subsequently coats the exterior of the organism, which helps it evade phagocytosis.\u00a0 Although patients with CGD are at elevated risk for <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">S aureus</em>, most of the other common pathogens in CGD do not produce coagulase.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 Lecithinase (alpha toxin) is the major virulence factor of <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Clostridium perfringens</em>; it causes hydrolysis of membrane phospholipids, activating inflammatory pathways that increase platelet and leukocyte aggregation in the adjacent microvasculature, leading to vasoocclusion and ischemic necrosis.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 Lipopolysaccharide, a major virulence factor in the outer membrane of gram-negative bacteria, is not present in the gram-positive bacteria (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">S aureus</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nocardia</em>) and fungal organisms (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Aspergillus</em>) that usually infect patients with CGD.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 The polysaccharide capsule is a major virulence factor for <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Streptococcus pneumoniae</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neisseria meningitidis</em>, and certain strains of <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Haemophilus influenzae</em>.\u00a0 Its primary role is to inhibit opsonophagocytosis.\u00a0 Many of the common pathogens in CGD (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nocardia</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Aspergillus</em>) do not contain a polysaccharide capsule.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Chronic granulomatous disease is a primary immunodeficiency due to impaired NADPH oxidase, an enzyme that generates reactive oxygen species in phagolysosomes.\u00a0 Diminished intracellular killing within neutrophils leads to susceptibility to recurrent infection with catalase-producing bacteria (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Staphylococcus aureus</em>, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nocardia</em>) and fungi (eg, <em style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Aspergillus</em>).\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Chronic granulomatous disease is a primary immunodeficiency due to impaired NADPH oxidase, an enzyme that generates reactive oxygen species in phagolysosomes.  Diminished intracellular killing within neutrophils leads to susceptibility to recurrent infection with catalase-producing bacteria (eg, Staphylococcus aureus , Nocardia ) and fungi (eg, Aspergillus ).\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c", "subject": "Immunology", "system": "Allergy & Immunology", "topic": "Primary immunodeficiency disorder", "category": "Immune deficiencies", "peerCorrect": 52.0}